"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "5273"} "1,500 metres Freestyle, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "5307"} "4 × 200 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "5282"} "100 metres Backstroke, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "5295"} "200 metres Breaststroke, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "5325"} "100 metres Freestyle, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "5337"} "400 metres Freestyle, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "5365"} "4 × 100 metres Freestyle Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "5354"} "200 metres Breaststroke, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "4816"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "4915"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "5010"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "5109"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "5217"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "5459"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "5605"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "5790"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "6066"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "6370"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "6648"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "6888"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "7164"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "7505"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "7860"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "8207"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "8606"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "8996"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261735"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "322120"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "357226"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000238"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2001744"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/595"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "100 metres Backstroke, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "29 – 31 July 1952"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/375"} "Helsingin Uimastadion, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/5348"} "20 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "There was a clear favourite for the 100m Backstroke in the form of the eighteen year old Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/49429"} "Geertje Wielema"] "  but Wielema was taken ill with anaemia and barely trained in the months before the Games. Despite these problems Wielema set an Olympic record in the semi-final. The final turned into a straight battle between Wielema and sixteen year old " [:a {:href "/athletes/49976"} "Joan Harrison"] "  of South Africa who had narrowly missed a medal in the 100m freestyle. Wielema and Harrison, swimming in lanes four and five respectively were level as they approached the wall but Harrison’s finish was better and the decision of the judges was to award the gold to the South African.  It was a desperately close finish and not all of the officials were in agreement. Wielema herself believed she a quick glance to see where her rival was may have cost the vital fraction of a second needed for her to win. Dutch disappointment was compounded when " [:a {:href "/athletes/49611"} "Jean Stewart"] "  of New Zealand beat " [:a {:href "/athletes/49318"} "Joke de Korte"] "  to the bronze in another extremely close finish and also when " [:a {:href "/athletes/49401"} "Ria van der Horst"] "  was disqualified by making an illegal turn. Harrison won four medals at the 1954 Commonwealth Games before retiring at the age of just seventeen while Wielema was both European champion and Dutch Sportsperson of the year for the year 1954. Wielema would have been a strong contender for further Olympic honours in 1956 had it not been for the withdrawal of the Dutch team."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {}